  "description": "SOTJOB crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C54 H64 Dy6 N4 O40 2+,C54 H64 Dy6 N4 O40 2+,4(N1 O3 1-),6(C3 H6 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy4A (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors; Dy6A (Dy) has 9 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.504-3.748 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.81-110.54°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C63H86Dy6N6O50. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
